  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "By reason of its bulk, mass, scale, and design, the proposed development would result in a disproportionately large roof that creates a top-heavy appearance. This would erode the symmetrical roof form of the terrace and give rise to an overly bulky and dominant dwelling that is incongruous with the modest scale of surrounding properties. The impact is further exacerbated when considered alongside the existing development on site, resulting in a visually intrusive and discordant addition that constitutes overdevelopment.&nbsp;As such, the proposed development is contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024) Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)"
  ],
